  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias during high volatility regimes; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 5-10% when recent history shows a spike (e.g., >83 EUR).",
    "Apply aggressive mean reversion correction: reduce forecasted path by approximately 6-8 EUR immediately following a historical peak to account for rapid downside reversals.",
    "Ignore sentiment spikes in the last 2 days; they do not correlate with future price direction and should be treated as noise when generating long-term forecasts.",
    "Forecast horizon error is non-linear: model assumes smooth growth but true outcomes show sharp drops within the first 10 days followed by a slow recovery, requiring a concave downward adjustment to the forecast curve.",
    "When recent history volatility (standard deviation) exceeds 2.5 EUR, reduce forecast confidence and apply a floor correction of -7 EUR from the model's projected average."
  ]
}
